From: Julian Decker <git@deckerjulian.com>
Subject: drm/rockchip: dw_hdmi: handle a missing PHY in late_register

hdmi->phy comes from devm_phy_optional_get(), so it is NULL on SoCs that
drive the PHY inside the DesignWare controller, RK3399 among them.
dw_hdmi_encoder_late_register() read hdmi->phy->debugfs regardless, which
is a NULL pointer fault while the DRM device registers.

Look at phy->debugfs only when there is a PHY. Without one the directory is
still created: the controller's status and ctrl files do not depend on a
PHY, and the "phy" file in it is made for exactly the internal PHY. Nothing
has to keep the dentry then, the directory lives under the DRM device's own
debugfs root and is removed with it.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
@@ -2072,9 +2072,12 @@
 	 * The HDMI PHY driver clears the debugfs node registered by the PHY
 	 * framework during probe so that the HDMI controller can pass its
 	 * HDMI debugfs directory (/sys/kernel/debug/dri/0/hdmiX/) to the
-	 * PHY driver via phy->debugfs.
+	 * PHY driver via phy->debugfs. Without a separate PHY the directory
+	 * belongs to the DRM device alone and goes away with it.
 	 */
-	if (!hdmi->phy->debugfs)
+	if (!hdmi->phy)
+		dw_hdmi_register_debugfs(hdmi->hdmi);
+	else if (!hdmi->phy->debugfs)
 		hdmi->phy->debugfs = dw_hdmi_register_debugfs(hdmi->hdmi);
 	dw_hdmi_phy_init(hdmi->hdmi);
 
